    "intro_html":  "Thai green curry is built the proper way here, which means the paste gets fried in the thick cream at the top of the coconut milk can until the oil breaks out and the kitchen smells like a Bangkok side street. That one step separates a real curry from a can of soup with chicken in it. Eggplant, snow peas and a fistful of basil go in at the end. Each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
